From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: resources shared with Venus (VIOGPU_RES_ATTACH)

The D3D12 driver's swap chain buffers are Venus images on the memory of their own kernel allocation's host texture
(VIRGL_BIND_VK_SHARED, virglrenderer image patch 0012). Venus imports that memory by resource id, and the host looks
the id up in the Venus context, which runs on a kernel device of its own that never opens the allocation. An escape
on that device, VIOGPU_RES_ATTACH, attaches the resource to its context - only resources created with
VIRGL_BIND_VK_SHARED (the adapter keeps their ids), anything else would hand another process's textures over.
---
diff --git a/viogpu/common/virgl_hw.h b/viogpu/common/virgl_hw.h
index 7055564..6ef0d2b 100644
--- a/viogpu/common/virgl_hw.h
+++ b/viogpu/common/virgl_hw.h
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 #define VIRGL_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET           (1 << 7)
 #define VIRGL_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET           (1 << 7)
 #define VIRGL_BIND_SCANOUT                  (1 << 18)
+// WinBoat (virglrenderer image patch 0012): a texture the guest also renders to through Venus
+#define VIRGL_BIND_VK_SHARED                (1 << 13)
 
 // Blt command specification for kernel BLTs
 #define VIRGL_CMD0(cmd, obj, len)           ((cmd) | ((obj) << 8) | ((len) << 16))
